Chapter: Bezier

  cites Foreword chapter MathLib

 Bezier curves (quadratic and cubic) using fixed-point (scale 1000).
 Evaluates points along curves, computes arc length approximations,
 and splits curves at arbitrary t values. Control points are integer
 fixed-point BezVec values (not the Real Vec3 of Quaternion), so the
 whole pipeline stays in integer arithmetic.

 We say:

Section: Types
  BezVec = record {
    vx : Integer,
    vy : Integer,
    vz : Integer
  }

 The weights cannot be represented. At a t of 250 the true cubic weights are
 .421875, .421875, .140625 and .015625, whose fractional parts sum to exactly
 three; at scale 1000 truncating each loses those three and rounding each gains
 one, so no per-weight rounding makes them sum to 1000. Computed as they were,
 they summed to 996 and every point on the curve was pulled four parts in a
 thousand toward the origin. Summing the products before dividing, which was
 the first fix, removes one truncation per control point and leaves this one:
 the degenerate curve was still 99, 199, 298 at a t of 250.

Section: Interpolation
  bez-lerp : BezVec, BezVec, Integer -> BezVec
  bez-lerp (p) (q) (t) =
    BezVec { vx = p.vx + (q.vx - p.vx) * t / 1000, vy = p.vy + (q.vy - p.vy) * t / 1000, vz = p.vz + (q.vz - p.vz) * t / 1000 }

Section: Quadratic
  bezier2-eval : BezVec, BezVec, BezVec, Integer -> BezVec
  bezier2-eval (p0) (p1) (p2) (t) =
    bez-lerp (bez-lerp p0 p1 t) (bez-lerp p1 p2 t) t

Section: Cubic
  bezier3-eval : BezVec, BezVec, BezVec, BezVec, Integer -> BezVec
  bezier3-eval (p0) (p1) (p2) (p3) (t) =
    let ab = bez-lerp p0 p1 t
    in let bc = bez-lerp p1 p2 t
    in let cd = bez-lerp p2 p3 t
    in bez-lerp (bez-lerp ab bc t) (bez-lerp bc cd t) t

Section: Sampling
  bezier3-sample : BezVec, BezVec, BezVec, BezVec, Integer -> List BezVec
  bezier3-sample (p0) (p1) (p2) (p3) (steps) = bezier3-sample-loop p0 p1 p2 p3 0 steps []

  bezier3-sample-loop : BezVec, BezVec, BezVec, BezVec, Integer, Integer, List BezVec -> List BezVec
  bezier3-sample-loop (p0) (p1) (p2) (p3) (i) (steps) (acc) =
    if i > steps then acc
    else let t = i * 1000 / steps
    in bezier3-sample-loop p0 p1 p2 p3 (i + 1) steps (list-push acc (bezier3-eval p0 p1 p2 p3 t))

Section: Arc Length Approximation
  bezier3-arc-length : BezVec, BezVec, BezVec, BezVec, Integer -> Integer
  bezier3-arc-length (p0) (p1) (p2) (p3) (segments) = bezier3-arc-loop p0 p1 p2 p3 0 segments 0 (bezier3-eval p0 p1 p2 p3 0)

  bezier3-arc-loop : BezVec, BezVec, BezVec, BezVec, Integer, Integer, Integer, BezVec -> Integer
  bezier3-arc-loop (p0) (p1) (p2) (p3) (i) (segments) (total) (prev) =
    if i >= segments then total
    else let t = (i + 1) * 1000 / segments
    in let curr = bezier3-eval p0 p1 p2 p3 t
    in let dx = curr.vx - prev.vx
    in let dy = curr.vy - prev.vy
    in let dist = math-isqrt (dx * dx + dy * dy)
    in bezier3-arc-loop p0 p1 p2 p3 (i + 1) segments (total + dist) curr

Section: Formatting
  format-bezier-point : BezVec -> Text
  format-bezier-point (v) = "(" & show (v.vx) & "," & show (v.vy) & ")"

